--TEST--
`Core\Response::stream` throws for a negative length and for an etag a header cannot carry, and `offset()` and `length()` throw on a stream without a length -- `rule:http-server/static-serving-is-one-policy`
--FILE--
<?nvs
try {
    Core\Response::stream("text/plain", -1);
} catch (LogicError $negative) {
    echo $negative->message, "\n";
}
try {
    Core\Response::stream("text/plain", 1, "v\"1");
} catch (LogicError $quoted) {
    echo $quoted->message, "\n";
}

var $chunked = Core\Response::stream("text/plain");
try {
    $chunked->offset();
} catch (LogicError $noOffset) {
    echo $noOffset->message, "\n";
}
try {
    $chunked->length();
} catch (LogicError $noLength) {
    echo $noLength->message, "\n";
}

// A length of 0 is a body with no bytes, and a valid one.
var $empty = Core\Response::stream("text/plain", 0, "v1");
echo $empty->offset(), " ", $empty->length(), "\n";
--EXPECT--
Core\Response::stream(): the length -1 is negative. It must be 0 or more.
Core\Response::stream(): the etag `v"1` cannot be sent in an `ETag` header. It must be printable ASCII and must not contain `"`.
Core\Response\Stream::offset(): the stream was started without a `$length`.
Core\Response\Stream::length(): the stream was started without a `$length`.
0 0
